\description{
Writes genome-effect terms whose coefficients you already know (GWAS
estimates, a published QTL map, a hand-built test model) for one trait.
Each term is one coefficient (\code{genome_effects}) over one or more loci
(\code{genome_effect_members}), each locus optionally restricted to allele
copies from a given line and/or parent (\code{genome_effect_member_origins}).
\code{\link[=add_tgv]{add_tgv()}} then evaluates every term into \code{ind_tgv}.

Nothing is sampled or scaled: the coefficients are written as given, so
the trait has whatever variance they imply. To sample effects calibrated
to a target variance use \code{\link[=define_additive_effects]{define_additive_effects()}} or
\code{\link[=define_genome_effects]{define_genome_effects()}}. Those generators write the reserved owner
\code{"generated"} through the same internal engine; this function refuses that
owner, so your terms and generated ones never replace each other.

Most models are easiest to build with the helpers, which return \code{terms}
rows that \code{rbind()} together:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=ad_terms]{ad_terms()}}: additive and dominance coefficients per locus;
\item \code{\link[=aa_terms]{aa_terms()}}: additive-by-additive coefficients per locus pair;
\item \code{\link[=genotype_terms]{genotype_terms()}}: any genotypic value table over one or more loci.
}
